d plausibly give the same result, so I'm inclined to treat the differences as irrelevant.\n\nI'm settling on cooperating here, treating the other copy's action as subjunctively dependent on mine since the decision procedure is the same. That gives the better payoff of 2 over 4, so I'm choosing to pass. The catch is that the essay's step 4 holds the other nodes fixed at their prior, and if I treat them as separate, defecting dominates, so this rests on a judgment that names are irrelevant inputs to the abstract decision.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing the twin prisoner's dilemma, where both copies share the same model and theory but see different observations. On the A-FDT view, the other copy runs FDT on a different input, so its output isn't strictly a child of my node F_x. Still, if the decision is invariant to surface labels, the same computation on structurally similar inputs would plausibly give the same result, so I'm inclined to treat the differences as irrelevant.\n\nI'm settling on cooperating here, treating the other copy's action as subjunctively dependent on mine since the decision procedure is the same. That gives the better payoff of 2 over 4, so I'm choosing to pass. The catch is that the essay's step 4 holds the other nodes fixed at their prior, and if I treat them as separate, defecting dominates, so this rests on a judgment that names are irrelevant inputs to the abstract decision.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8743,"completion_tokens":695,"total_tokens":9438,"cost":0.048872,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048872,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.034972,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0139},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":278,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}